  "footnotes": [
    "[a] A solution of fluoroiodomethane (1) (0.10 M in THF; flow rate: 4.0 mL/min) and a solution of MeLi (Br free; 0.20 M in Et2O; flow rate: 4.0 mL/min) or LDA (0.42 M in THF; flow rate: 1.0 mL min-1) were introduced to M1 by syringe pumps. The resulting solution was passed through R1 (tR1 = 0.013 s, T = -60 °C (4a-i); tR1 = 0.082 s, T = -40 °C (5a-c, 6a-c)) and was mixed with a solution of electrophiles (0.30 M in THF) (flow rate: 4.0 mL min-1) in M2. The resulting solution was passed through R2 (tR2 = 7.85 s, T = -60 °C (4a-4i); tR2 = 10.47 s, T = -40 °C (5a-5c); tR2 = 20.94 s, T = -40 °C (6a-6c)).",
    "[b] Previous research data (Ref. [3a]).",
    "[c] Yields were determined by 1H NMR analysis using dibromomethane as an internal standard.",
    "[d] The productivity was calculated based on the yield of the isolated product."
